Silence is not merely a missing token. It can change:
  (1) EXPECTATION: what the receiver thinks should have appeared;
  (2) INFERENCE: what the receiver believes after it does not appear;
  (3) AUTHORSHIP: who supplies the next meaningful act;
  (4) POSSIBILITY: which future actions are available;
  (5) POWER: who can choose, refuse, wait, or withdraw;
  (6) OBSERVABILITY: which actual facts the receiver can detect.

Differentiate non-occurrence from unobserved occurrence; withheld data from
missing data; no action from lack of authorization; fixed completion from open
creation. Do not infer hidden agency simply because a gap feels meaningful.

